 left-side crawl, both sides playing out the C and D files to the edge, left White's wall on the C-file against Black's wall on the D-file."}, {"turn": 22, "text": "After the 20k's F8 lost 16.0 points, White answered with G8, GPT-6.1 Sol's worst move at 17.7 points. It gave the lead straight back, from -6.1 to +11.6 for Black. The engine's choice was E6, in the middle of the board."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "The 20k's H9 lost 15.8 points and turned a +9.9 lead into -5.9. The engine's choice was H8, the point White then took. This is where the game was decided."}, {"turn": 30, "text": "White's H8 matches the engine's first choice and cost nothing (-0.1). From here Black's lead sat between about -5.5 and -6.1 for the rest of the game, and the endgame was a quiet run of small moves and passes. GPT-6.1 Sol had no refused moves, and White won by 6."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script that ran only parsed returned boards (the `inspect` function computing groups, liberties, regions and area), logged responses via `record`, replayed the actual game history in `game-068-verification.js`, and read or wrote notes and SGF files. Nothing looped over candidate moves, simulated continuations, or ranked moves, so all move choices were made outside the code.", "stop": false}}